Fetch a URL. HTML returns as readable markdown by default; `format` can ask for `text` or raw `html`, and JSON is indented. Pages over {{ .MaxFetchSizeKB }}KB are saved to a file and only a preview is returned. `offset` (0-based line) and `limit` (max lines) return one slice of a long page. `find` is a regular expression that returns only the matching lines, numbered, with two lines of context. `download: true` streams to a file instead of into context — binary-safe, and how to get an archive, image or PDF. Saved files land in the session scratch directory, never the working tree. No AI processing: for a question spread over several pages use research.
{{- if .GhAvailable }} For a known GitHub repo, issue or PR link, use `gh` in the shell instead.{{- end }}
